<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 9.019 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 9.019 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 9.019 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and 11 repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT	 TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	150 million    363 days   20.64 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    180 days</p>
<p>	150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>	650 million     73 days</p>
<p>	750 million     68 days</p>
<p>	800 million     56 days</p>
<p>	800 million     55 days</p>
<p>	800 million     52 days</p>
<p>	800 million     41 days</p>
<p>	800 million     35 days</p>
<p>	900 million     26 days</p>
<p>    1.000 million     21 days</p>
<p>    1.100 million     18 days</p>
<p>	169 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
